This product orchestrates independent upstream physics tools (MadGraph5_aMC@NLO, Pythia8,
Delphes, Rivet, ATLAS SimpleAnalysis, RestFrames, pyhf, SModelS, MadAnalysis 5, LHAPDF),
each the work of its own authors under its own license — see THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md.

The public analysis catalogue contains factual identifiers, short metadata,
source locations and hashes derived from the Rivet and ATLAS SimpleAnalysis
projects and the pyhf public probability-model index. Upstream revisions and
links are recorded in the catalogue. Their routines, learned model files and
reference datasets are not incorporated as Ravel implementations. Catalogue
availability does not imply upstream endorsement or scientific validation.

Research orchestration calls LangGraph and its SQLite checkpoint saver under their MIT licenses.
LangGraph source: https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph ; core 1.2.14 and SQLite saver 3.1.1.
The required LangChain Core distribution supplies framework primitives; no wholesale LangChain agent migration is claimed.
No third-party framework source is vendored by this adapter.

The model-bound diagram adapters call the external FeynGraph implementation
(15afe2f2, MPL-2.0), HEPTAPOD NDA and Diagrammatica code/parser/converter
(705b03cc and separately retained cb771f8c, GNU GPL), and the external
FeynArts 3.12/FeynCalc 10.1.0 implementations under their original licenses.
Ravel authors the typed source/runtime transport and ordinary workflow joins,
not these upstream algorithms. Release notices, authors and licenses are
retained in src/ravel/data/diagram_tools and the existing HEPTAPOD source assets.
Published results using FeynArts must acknowledge its code as required by
the original release notice. The upstream packages remain separately provisioned.

Particle Data Group data (CC BY 4.0)
------------------------------------
src/ravel/data/reference/pdg holds a subset of the Particle Data Group Review of
Particle Physics, 2026 edition, generated from the offline database in the pdg
2026.0 package and licensed CC BY 4.0. Cite: Particle Data Group, Int. J. Mod.
Phys. A 41, 2630011 (2026). Edition, release time and checksums are recorded in
src/ravel/data/reference/pdg/SOURCE.json.

LHC Higgs Working Group reference tables (CC BY 4.0)
----------------------------------------------------
src/ravel/data/knowledge/higgs holds a table file extracted from two source documents (the PDFs themselves are not redistributed; they are fetched on demand and checked against their pinned sha256):
LHC Higgs Cross Section Working Group, "Handbook of LHC Higgs Cross Sections: 4.
Deciphering the Nature of the Higgs Sector", CERN Yellow Reports: Monographs, CERN-2017-002,
doi:10.23731/CYRM-2017-002, arXiv:1610.07922; and LHC Higgs Working Group, "Ad interim
recommendations for the Higgs boson production cross sections at sqrt(s) = 13.6 TeV",
LHCHWG-2024-001, arXiv:2402.09955. Both are licensed CC BY 4.0. The extracted values
are copied from the printed tables; table locators, byte sizes and sha256 checksums are in
SOURCE.json. Cite the Yellow Report together with the 13.6 TeV note when using 13.6 TeV values.

MCFM amplitude add-on (separately licensed)
-------------------------------------------
The Fortran driver, capture module, lowint patch and CMake adaptation in
addons/gpl/mcfm-amplitudes adapt MCFM 10.2.1, commit
0adaa4ed4079de1b17c84417a0a428a468f57e69, and are licensed GPL-3.0-or-later.
They are not part of the RAVEL Python package. The installer fetches MCFM,
applies the overlay and builds it as a separate program; RAVEL exchanges only
files with that program. MCFM original source: Copyright (C) 2019-2022,
respective authors of MCFM; original gg_ZZ assembly author J. M. Campbell.
The add-on directory holds the GPLv3 text and an attribution note.
